// Codegen root for the Rust binding. Not part of the wire contract: it
// declares no types, no root_type and no file_identifier, and nothing
// includes it.
//
// flatc's --rust-module-root-file writes one mod.rs per root file it is given,
// each covering that root and its includes, all to the same path — so the last
// root silently wins. With delta.fbs and snapshot.fbs both roots and neither
// including the other, the winner's mod.rs declares only its own half of the
// tree, which is how delta_generated.rs came to be generated but left
// undeclared (and so fbs::Delta unreachable from Rust).
//
// This file is passed last, after the real schemas, so the mod.rs that wins is
// one covering every type. It cannot replace them in the command: flatc emits
// code only for the roots it is given, and a root with no types of its own
// emits nothing but the mod.rs. --gen-all would emit the included types, but it
// treats them as dependencies and drops their root accessors (root_as_snapshot,
// finish_delta_buffer, the file identifiers) — exactly the API the wire layer
// needs. Hence: every schema a root, this one last.
//
// Add a new .fbs to engine/schema and it goes in two places: the flatc
// arguments in scripts/schema.sh, and the include list here.
//
// The Go binding needs no counterpart: flatc's Go output is one file per type
// with no module root to overwrite.
include "common.fbs";
include "delta.fbs";
include "snapshot.fbs";
